== What this means ==
#
# The 1.32.0 provider imports exactly two CUDA-major DLLs by base name:
# cublasLt64_13.dll and cublas64_13.dll (plus onnxruntime_providers_shared.dll,
# dxgi and the MSVC runtime). cuDNN, cuFFT and cudart are resolved at run time,
# so dumpbin does not list them; the provider's own load does.
#
# Resolve 21.2 ships CUDA 12 beside Resolve.exe, so a plain install offers no
# cublas64_13.dll: the load fails with error 1114 and the host reports nothing
# more specific. On the machine this was measured on, the CUDA 13.0 toolkit is
# on PATH, so cublas64_13.dll resolves from
# C:\Program Files\NVIDIA GPU Computing Toolkit\CUDA\v13.0\bin\x64 - and the
# same bundle did load and run in Resolve (label "all nodes on CUDA"). That run
# is a separate case, not evidence that Resolve's own CUDA stack accepts 13.
#
# Not measured: the 1114 path inside the host. The attempt to strip the toolkit
# from the host's PATH ended in the host's script-server flakiness ("Failed to
# connect to script server", ioctlsocket err 1), so the refusal is documented
# from the import table and from our own gate, not from a host log. Loading the
# provider DLL standalone cannot answer it either: its DllMain expects the ORT
# core's mailbox and fails with 1114 regardless (onnx-and-tensorrt.md section 3).
